From 378021515a37ff29f5126332c8a9aa8bbf659a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:11:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(drilling): judge a cross drill against the finished part

A cross (radial) drill was never checked against the part it leaves:
on a solid bar with no modelled hole, or past a modelled hole's floor,
it posted a hole the finished part does not have. The reach, spindle
and rapid laws judge where the drill stands and travels, not what it
cuts.

The cross arm now sweeps the finished chain - the drill's radius along
the hole axis from the station to the tip, the point cone, shank and
holder, posed along each move's tool axis - through the part's solid
(the verify crate's solid law, the axial verdict's 0.01 mm gouge
tolerance), and refuses by name: the hole, how deep the tip got, and
whether the model has no hole there or the drill runs past its floor.
The refusal is a generation error, so nothing reaches the post.

The cross suites drilled solid bars with no modelled hole; they now
model their holes (tests/punched_bar). The bar is longer (z -80..20,
top unchanged) and each hole carries its half-turn image, because the
lathe axis reader refuses an r10 x 40 bar with a cross hole (#152,
not touched here). Decisions in RECOMMENDED.md.

Pinned by drilling_cross_part: a_cross_drill_into_a_solid_bar_is_refused_by_name,
a_cross_hole_deeper_than_the_modelled_hole_is_refused,
a_cross_hole_matching_its_modelled_hole_is_clean.

Fixes #117

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
